WEBVTT

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:15.238
After reopening the file, double-click Assembly in the tree to activate it—only then are the joint buttons available

00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:24.538
Joints tell FreeCAD how parts connect. For each joint: click the joint button, pick one element (circular edge, face) on each of two parts, OK

00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:34.739
Revolute: the bearing bore edge on the frame, then the matching edge on the shaft—the shaft can only turn about its axis

00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:44.938
Revolute: the end edge of the crank pin, the big-end bore edge of the rod—the rod rides on the crank pin

00:00:44.938 --> 00:00:55.339
Revolute: the rod's small-end bore and the pin on the needle-bar link

00:00:55.339 --> 00:01:05.539
Slider: the bush bore edge and a needle-bar edge—the bar can only slide along its axis

00:01:05.539 --> 00:01:17.539
With four joints the parts are all in place. Count: the crank can turn (1 DOF) and the rod and needle bar follow—the whole mechanism has 1 degree of freedom
